{"title":"Number Of Sets Of K Non Overlapping Line Segments","difficulty":"Medium","statement":"Given n points on a 1-D plane, where the ith point (from 0 to n-1) is at x = i, find the number of ways we can draw exactly k non-overlapping line segments such that each segment covers two or more points. The endpoints of each segment must have integral coordinates. The k line segments do not have to cover all n points, and they are allowed to share endpoints.\nReturn the number of ways we can draw k non-overlapping line segments. Since this number can be huge, return it modulo 10^9 + 7.\n\n## Examples\n\n### Example 1\n\n```text\nInput: n = 4, k = 2\nOutput: 5\n```\n\nThe five valid endpoint-pair sets are {(0,2),(2,3)}, {(0,1),(1,3)}, {(0,1),(2,3)}, {(1,2),(2,3)}, and {(0,1),(1,2)}.\n\n### Example 2\n\n```text\nInput: n = 3, k = 1\nOutput: 3\n```\n\nThe 3 ways are {(0,1)}, {(0,2)}, {(1,2)}.\n\n### Example 3\n\n```text\nInput: n = 30, k = 7\nOutput: 796297179\n```\n\nThe total number of possible ways to draw 7 line segments is 3796297200. Taking this number modulo 10^9 + 7 gives us 796297179.\n\n## Constraints\n\n- 2 <= n <= 1000\n- 1 <= k <= n-1\n\n## Output Contract\n\nReturn the number of valid segment sets modulo 10^9 + 7.","starterCode":"class Solution:\n    def numberOfSets(self, n: int, k: int) -> int:\n        pass\n","entryPoint":"Solution().numberOfSets","parameters":[{"name":"n","type":"int"},{"name":"k","type":"int"}],"returnType":"int","tests":[{"input":[1000,999],"expected":1},{"input":[102,51],"expected":493585155},{"input":[103,54],"expected":777698210},{"input":[104,61],"expected":453140365},{"input":[105,101],"expected":1414910},{"input":[105,34],"expected":354224599},{"input":[105,46],"expected":267054047},{"input":[105,90],"expected":733559008},{"input":[109,26],"expected":773191195},{"input":[109,77],"expected":233017065},{"input":[109,90],"expected":727100239},{"input":[11,6],"expected":1820},{"input":[113,13],"expected":920147501},{"input":[113,39]